<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI50-WINDOWS-DAEMON-SINGLETON-SMOKE-MERGEFORWARD-REGRESSION>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI50-WINDOWS-DAEMON-SINGLETON-SMOKE-MERGEFORWARD-REGRESSION" ;
  triage:title "New Windows Test-leg regression on feature/pAI-s50-fuzz-report introduced by merge commit 4bf711cf (isolated shared-host singleton smoke)" ;
  triage:description """PR #709 (branch feature/pAI-s50-fuzz-report). quality-mgr, while independently checking `gh pr checks 709` after AI50-QA-3 verified the unrelated AI50-WINDOWS-PATH-ASSERTION-MERGEFORWARD-GAP fix, found the `Test (windows-latest)` job now fails: run 30683653213 (head 4bf711cf), step "Run isolated shared-host singleton smoke" (step #16), job 91325416321. Failure tail (~lines 2428-2442 of the raw log): `RuntimeError: {... "stderr": "failed to read daemon HTTP headers: An existing connection was forcibly closed by the remote host. (os error 10054)\\n  Recovery: Ensure atm-daemon binary is installed, then restore the single local daemon to a healthy serving state and retry."`. On the prior commit ccfb3c99 (run 30683040652), the same `Test (windows-latest)` job's conclusion was "success" -- this is a NEW regression on 4bf711cf, not a pre-existing/carry-forward failure on feature/pAI-s50-fuzz-report itself. Commit 4bf711cf is Cipher-311d's merge of origin/integrate/phase-ai-31-33 into feature/pAI-s50-fuzz-report, bringing in 35e6762d (Merge PR #707), 8b78775c (test(smoke) mock transport), 7384522d (chore(triage) close 2 findings), 6fcbf3ea (test(smoke) portable paths). Cross-check performed: PR #707's own CI (run 30682180647, the commit that became integrate/phase-ai-31-33's tip 35e6762d) shows `Test (windows-latest)` as PASS -- so the failure is not simply inherited/carried forward from integrate/phase-ai-31-33's already-green state; something in how those commits combine with feature/pAI-s50-fuzz-report's own tree on 4bf711cf triggers it. The failing step ("isolated shared-host singleton smoke") is unrelated to scripts/smoke/test_run_admission_capacity.py, the file touched by the AI50-WINDOWS-PATH-ASSERTION-MERGEFORWARD-GAP fix that motivated the merge -- so this looks like an emergent interaction from the merge rather than a direct edit to the failing test. Flake-precedent check: searched .triage/**/*.ttl and repo git log for prior "os error 10054" / "singleton smoke" / "isolated shared-host singleton" occurrences -- none found. No retry/rerun of run 30683653213 was observed at triage time. Given (a) clean bisection to a single merge commit, (b) no prior flake precedent for this exact symptom in triage history, and (c) the error being a Windows daemon-connection reset during a singleton-lifecycle smoke step (plausible timing/resource sensitivity on windows-latest runners), this is provisionally assessed as a genuine regression pending one CI rerun to rule out transient runner flake; if a rerun of the same commit passes cleanly, downgrade root-cause assessment to Windows CI flake and re-triage severity.""" ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "windows-ci-regression" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "waived" ;
  triage:closed true ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-08-01T04:35:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:closureNote "AI50-QA-3: rerun of the same commit (gh run rerun 30683653213 --failed) produced a clean PASS on Test (windows-latest) (job 91326228791), with the rest of the run unaffected (all 8 PR #709 CI legs green: ubuntu/macos/windows Test, Clippy, ubuntu/macos/windows Just lint, Format check). No code, config, or CI workflow change was made between the failing run and the passing rerun on head 4bf711cf -- same commit, same tree. This confirms the os error 10054 daemon-connection-reset in 'Run isolated shared-host singleton smoke' was a transient windows-latest runner flake, not a genuine regression introduced by the merge-forward commit. Waived rather than reopened as a real defect; downstream teams should watch for recurrence of this exact symptom (first documented occurrence of 'os error 10054' / singleton-smoke flake in phase-AI triage history) but no fix action is required on feature/pAI-s50-fuzz-report." ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-31T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AI50 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-07-31T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI50-WINDOWS-DAEMON-SINGLETON-SMOKE-MERGEFORWARD-REGRESSION/1> ;
  triage:relatedFinding "AI50-WINDOWS-PATH-ASSERTION-MERGEFORWARD-GAP" ;
  triage:rootCause "Windows-latest runner flake (transient os error 10054 daemon-connection reset) during 'Run isolated shared-host singleton smoke'; confirmed non-reproducing via clean same-commit rerun (job 91326228791). Not a code regression from merge commit 4bf711cf." ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "2" .

